{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore"]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"externalID":"s:11Persistence12SegmentStoreV","role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Persistence\/SegmentStore.swift#L78","fileName":"SegmentStore.swift"},"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"SegmentStore","modules":[{"name":"Persistence"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" that keeps records in a directory of append-only segment files, bounded in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"size, until they are delivered.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Stores","title":"Stores","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStoreError","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"]}],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Persistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(events:directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/byteCount","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/directory","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/append(_:)","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/takeRecoveredRecords()"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Properties","title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultByteBound","doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/defaultDirectory"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SegmentStore"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let store = try SegmentStore()","let tracker = Tracker(store: store)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: vendor)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Write-through."}]},{"text":" A tracker’s worker writes each record as it reaches it, before publishing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it, with one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"write()"},{"text":", off the tracking caller’s thread, so the record survives the app","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"crashing or being killed from then on. The store makes the log durable against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"power loss too (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fsync"},{"text":") once per batch, before the batch is delivered, and whenever","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/synchronize()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is called: call it, after the tracker’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flush()"},{"text":", as the app moves to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"background or terminates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A record whose write fails (the disk is full, say) is kept in memory only, and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/writeFailed(recordCount:timestamps:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", and so is one whose event’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"text":" throws.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"What is kept.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" Every event ","type":"text"},{"code":"DiscoveredEvent.all","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" structs of every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module the program links and the library’s own, or only the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types in ","type":"text"},{"code":"events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Events of any other type are kept in memory only: they are delivered in this run like any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other, are never written, and are lost if the app ends first. The first record of each such","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type is reported as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/notPersisted(event:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", so a type left out by mistake,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"such as one that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by hand, shows up.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A recovered record’s session."}]},{"text":" A record keeps the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":" of its context, written in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the record’s own bytes, so a record recovered after a relaunch carries the session it was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracked in, and a vendor destination sends it under the same identity as the first time. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record written without a session comes back with none. The rest of its context is not kept:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a recovered record is otherwise in the top-level ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"text":", as its span ended with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the earlier run.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Deleting."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" A segment is deleted as a whole once every record in it is delivered, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"log whose records are all delivered holds no files. A record’s session goes with its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"segment: the store keeps no session apart from the records tracked in it. A segment kept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for one undelivered record keeps its delivered ones too, sessions and all. Only recovery"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rewrites a segment: one still holding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records after it drops some ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)"},{"type":"text","text":") is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rewritten without them, so each drop is reported once. Should the rewrite fail, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"segment is kept as it was and the next launch reports those drops again."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading back.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" When a destination’s full buffer drops a batch on its way through a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivery, the delivery reads that batch’s records back from the log once the destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has caught up, reading each segment they are in once, and hands them to it in this run,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each in the context it was tracked in, which the delivery keeps. A record the bound dropped","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before the read finished isn’t read back, and one that can’t be read or decoded is logged","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and waits for a later launch.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Bound."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The log never holds more than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"byteBound"},{"text":" bytes. When a record wouldn’t fit, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"oldest segments are deleted until it does, and each one deleted with records not yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered yields a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/dropReports"},{"text":". A record too large for an empty log","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is kept in memory only.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Recovery."}]},{"type":"text","text":" A store opened on a directory recovers the records earlier runs left there"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a tracker given the store delivers them first. Each segment is cut at its first torn or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"corrupt record, keeping every intact record before it, and the bytes cut off are reported."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A segment comes back whole, delivered records and all. Each record a delivery had started on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comes back with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":" set, as it may have reached a destination already: one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered before the app ended, or one delivered just as it ended, before the store could"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delete its segment. A record whose delivery mark can’t be written is held back from that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery, so it is never sent twice unannounced, and delivered on a later launch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Other versions.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" A segment a newer release of the app wrote, in a later version of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format, is left on disk untouched after a rollback, for that release to deliver: this one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neither reads it nor counts it toward the bound. A segment in an earlier version, which this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one can’t read, is deleted and reported as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/corruption(byteCount:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Changed event types."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Each record’s event is a map of its properties by name, so a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written before its type changed still reads: a property removed since is skipped, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional one added since is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and one with a default value added since has it. A record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stored at another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event.schemaVersion"},{"type":"text","text":" than its type’s now is dropped without being read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/versionMismatch(event:storedVersion:currentVersion:recordCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"One at the same version that can’t be read all the same, after a required property was added"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or a property’s type changed without raising the version, is dropped and reported as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport\/undecodable(recordCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Open one store per directory at a time; two would delete each other’s segments. Copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"store share its log.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/pendingRecordCount":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How many records the log keeps that are not yet delivered."}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"pendingRecordCount","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/pendingRecordCount","type":"topic","title":"pendingRecordCount","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/pendingrecordcount","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/SegmentStore/init(directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)":{"type":"topic","title":"init(directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/SegmentStore\/init(directory:byteBound:segmentByteCount:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A store keeping events of every type the program declares with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":", and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library’s own, in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directory"},{"type":"text","text":"; it recovers the records already there."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/segmentstore\/init(directory:bytebound:segmentbytecount:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"directory","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FilePath","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SystemPackage8FilePathV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"byteBound","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"segmentByteCount","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentStoreError","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Persistence17SegmentStoreErrorO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/RecordStore":{"abstract":[{"text":"Where a tracker keeps each record until it is delivered, so records survive the app ending.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RecordStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/RecordStore","title":"RecordStore","url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/recordstore","role":"symbol"},"doc://Persistence/documentation/Persistence/DropReport":{"url":"\/documentation\/persistence\/dropreport","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Persistence\/documentation\/Persistence\/DropReport","title":"DropReport","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Records a store dropped before they were delivered, and why."}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DropReport"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Persistence/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier